title: Second Emergency Decree for Economy and Finance
subtitle: Chancellor [+ chancellor +] enacts his most controversial emergency decree yet.
new-page: true
view-if: total_bruning_time == 15 and bruning_toleration_time and war_loans >= 0 and not hoover_moratorium_seen and not emergency_act_alt_seen and not lautenbach_adopted and not bruning_sigma_time and not bruning_skibidi_time
on-arrival: emergency_decree_seen = 1; ddp_right += 3; gold_right += 5; lvp_right += 3; ddp_cohesion -= 3; pro_republic -= 5; burgher_royalist += burgher_ddp*0.2; guild_royalist += guild_ddp*0.2; burgher_royalist += burgher_gold*0.2; guild_royalist += guild_gold*0.2; burgher_ddp *= 0.6; guild_ddp *= 0.6; burgher_gold *= 0.6; guild_gold *= 0.6; burgher_royalist += burgher_lvp*0.2; guild_royalist += guild_lvp*0.2; burgher_lvp *= 0.8; guild_lvp *= 0.8; dufour_angry_bruning += 10; liberal_cooperation -= 3; bourgeois_cooperation -= 3; traditionalist_angry += 1 if marcher_toleration_right
tags: event
face-image: img/article48.jpg
max-visits: 1

= Second Emergency Decree for Economy and Finance

Intended to eliminate the growing deficit in the national budget, the emergency decree enacts sweeping cuts to government spending while introducing a special “crisis tax” and raising various other taxes. To justify the hardships imposed on Commonwealth society, Askew coupled its promulgation with a public appeal, urging the Commonwealth’s international creditors to acknowledge the sacrifices demanded of the Commonwealth people by providing relief from the nation’s “intolerable” War Loans burden.

The decree is deeply unpopular, provoking widespread outrage across Commonwealth society and fueling the intense agitation from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> against the bourgeois parties that still haven't split from Askew's government, particularly the [? if not lvp_formed: [? if gold_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and ?]<span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?], as they're the [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist:parties?][? if lvp_formed or not gold_exist:party?] representing the social groups most impacted by these changes. Askew's failure to consult [? if not lvp_formed:either party?][? if lvp_formed:them?] beforehand has left the [? if not lvp_formed:liberal parties?][? if lvp_formed: liberals?] powerless to amend some of the most severe provisions, such as cuts to civil servants' salaries and an increase in the national sales tax. [? if not lvp_formed and not bourgeois_parliament and not liberal_parliament and gold_exist: The already fragile alliance between the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and Askew appears to be on the verge of collapse—an outcome that could seal the fate of his government. ?]

- @nothing_to_do: There is nothing we can do.
- @vote_no
- @vote_yes

@nothing_to_do
view-if: marcher_toleration == 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.disfavored += 3;
Q.budget += 1;
Q.inflation -= 3;
Q.economic_growth -= 0.5;
Q.emergency_decree_mitigated = Q.liberal_parliament || (Q.bourgeois_parliament && !Q.lvp_formed) || Q.lvp_formed;
Q.emergency_decree_mitigated_more = Q.emergency_decree_mitigated && ((Q.lvp_leader == "Lytton" && Q.lvp_formed) || (Q.bourgeois_parliament && Q.bourgeois_parliament_ddp) || (Q.liberal_parliament && Q.liberal_cooperation >= 8));

if (Q.emergency_decree_mitigated) {
    Q.disfavored -= 1;
    Q.budget -= 1;
    Q.inflation += 1;
    Q.economic_growth += 0.3;
    Q.burgher_ddp += 3;
    Q.guild_ddp += 2;
    Q.burgher_gold += 4;
    Q.guild_gold += 4;
    Q.landed_gold += 2;
    Q.burgher_lvp += 6;
    Q.guild_lvp += 6;
    Q.landed_lvp += 2;
    Q.burgher_royalist -= 6;
    Q.guild_royalist -= 6;
    Q.gold_left += 5;
    Q.ddp_left += 3;
    Q.ddp_cohesion += 3;
    Q.lvp_left += 4;
}
if (Q.emergency_decree_mitigated_more) {
    Q.disfavored -= 0.2;
    Q.inflation += 0.2;
    Q.economic_growth += 0.1;
    Q.burgher_ddp += 2;
    Q.guild_ddp += 1;
    Q.burgher_gold += 2;
    Q.guild_gold += 2;
    Q.landed_gold += 1;
    Q.burgher_lvp += 3;
    Q.guild_lvp += 3;
    Q.landed_lvp += 1.5;
    Q.burgher_royalist -= 3;
    Q.guild_royalist -= 3;
    Q.gold_left += 3;
    Q.ddp_left += 1;
    Q.lvp_left += 2;
}
!}

The emergency policy passes under emergency rules, as the Assembly is currently dissolved. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> use this as a recruiting tool, and so do we. [? if bourgeois_parliament and not lvp_formed and not liberal_parliament: Fortunately, the bourgeois parliamentary group, with their leverage over Askew, has managed to persuade him to present President [+ president +] with a follow-up decree, reversing the most repugnant cuts that would threaten their electoral standing. [? if bourgeois_parliament_ddp: Furthermore, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s presence in the parliamentary group has led Vice-Chancellor and Finance Minister Dietrich of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to personally mitigate the severity of Askew's austerity measures.?]?][? if liberal_parliament: Fortunately, the liberal parliamentary group has allowed the liberal parties to combine their leverage over Askew, and persuade him to present President [+ president +] with a follow-up decree, reversing the most repugnant cuts that would threaten their electoral standing. [? if liberal_parliament and liberal_cooperation >= 8: Furthermore, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s Vice-Chancellor and Finance Minister Dietrich is able to personally mitigate the severity of Askew's austerity measures.?]?][? if lvp_formed: Fortunately, the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> with their leverage over Askew, has managed to persuade him to present President [+ president +] with a follow-up decree, reversing the most repugnant cuts that would threaten their electoral standing. [? if lvp_leader == "Lytton": Furthermore, the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>'s leader Hans Lytton is able to use his connections with Askew and the industrial community to influence his economic policy away from unrestrained austerity.?]?]

[? if not hoover_moratorium_seen: The one silver lining in this crisis is that with [+ chancellor +] announcing the Commonwealth’s inability to continue paying War Loans, <span style="color: #B31942;">United</span> <span style="color: #0A3161;">States</span> President Herbert Hoover has begun to lobby <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> to agree to a one-year suspension of payments. ?]

@vote_no
