We have broken with the [+ chancellor +] government, and have voted against them in a vote of no confidence. The decree has still been enacted, but at the very least, we are spared from bearing the full brunt of its effects ending our association with the [+ chancellor +]. [? if bourgeois_parliament and not lvp_formed and not liberal_parliament: Fortunately, the bourgeois parliamentary group, with their leverage over Askew, has managed to persuade him to present President [+ president +] with a follow-up decree, reversing the most repugnant cuts that would threaten their electoral standing. [? if bourgeois_parliament_ddp: Furthermore, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s presence in the parliamentary group has led Vice-Chancellor and Finance Minister Dietrich of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to personally mitigate the severity of Askew's austerity measures.?]?][? if liberal_parliament: Fortunately, the liberal parliamentary group has allowed the liberal parties to combine their leverage over Askew, and persuade him to present President [+ president +] with a follow-up decree, reversing the most repugnant cuts that would threaten their electoral standing. [? if liberal_parliament and liberal_cooperation >= 8: Furthermore, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s Vice-Chancellor and Finance Minister Dietrich is able to personally mitigate the severity of Askew's austerity measures.?]?][? if lvp_formed: Fortunately, the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> with their leverage over Askew, has managed to persuade him to present President [+ president +] with a follow-up decree, reversing the most repugnant cuts that would threaten their electoral standing. [? if lvp_leader == "Lytton": Furthermore, the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>'s leader Hans Lytton is able to use his connections with Askew and the industrial community to influence his economic policy away from unrestrained austerity.?]?]

